# A shell script with CRLF line endings does not run: the shebang line ends
# with a carriage return, and the interpreter it names is "/bin/bash\r" - a
# file that does not exist. The symptom is "bad interpreter" on every
# Windows checkout, because git converts line endings on the way out and
# nothing told it not to for these files.
#
# The scripts in this repository are run by a shell, on every platform
# including the ones where git checks them out with CRLF.
*.sh text eol=lf
